# backend/alembic/README
Hand-written Alembic revisions only — no --autogenerate.

## Filename pattern (KP)

```text
YYYY_MM_DD_HHMM_NNNN_slug.py
```

Example:

```text
2025_11_17_1522_0001_uuid_v7_base_setup.py
 └─date──┘└time┘└seq┘ └─ from: alembic revision -m "uuid_v7_base_setup" ─┘
```

`revision` in the file equals the filename stem. Sequence (`0001`, `0002`, …) is the
**fourth** numeric segment — not the `HHMM` time block.

Built by `build_migration_revision_id()` in `env.py` (`alembic.ini`: `file_template = %%(rev)s`).

## Commands

From `backend/`:

```bash
alembic revision -m "uuid_v7_base_setup"   # edit upgrade()/downgrade() by hand
alembic upgrade head
alembic -x test=true upgrade head           # uses TEST_DATABASE_URL
```
